1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,010
Allah calls

2
00:00:01,010 --> 00:00:02,926
it the best of stories.

3
00:00:02,926 --> 00:00:03,994
His whole story

4
00:00:03,994 --> 00:00:06,002
is told in a single surah,

5
00:00:06,002 --> 00:00:08,011
from beginning to end.

6
00:00:08,011 --> 00:00:10,031
This is the story of Yusuf,

7
00:00:10,031 --> 00:00:11,447
peace be upon him,

8
00:00:11,447 --> 00:00:12,504
told the way

9
00:00:12,504 --> 00:00:14,222
the Quran tells it.

10
00:00:14,222 --> 00:00:14,954
It begins

11
00:00:14,954 --> 00:00:17,118
with a boy and a dream.

12
00:00:17,148 --> 00:00:18,994
Yusuf said to his father,

13
00:00:18,994 --> 00:00:20,259
the prophet Yaqub,

14
00:00:20,259 --> 00:00:21,769
peace be upon him:

15
00:00:21,769 --> 00:00:23,290
O my father,

16
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:24,973
I saw eleven stars

17
00:00:24,973 --> 00:00:26,889
and the sun and the moon.

18
00:00:26,889 --> 00:00:29,227
I saw them prostrating to me.

19
00:00:29,338 --> 00:00:30,023
Yaqub knew

20
00:00:30,023 --> 00:00:30,999
what the dream meant,

21
00:00:30,999 --> 00:00:32,682
and he knew his sons.

22
00:00:32,682 --> 00:00:33,262
He said:

23
00:00:33,262 --> 00:00:34,482
O my son,

24
00:00:34,482 --> 00:00:35,294
do not tell

25
00:00:35,294 --> 00:00:36,989
your vision to your brothers,

26
00:00:36,989 --> 00:00:37,988
or they will plot

27
00:00:37,988 --> 00:00:39,200
against you.

28
00:00:39,241 --> 00:00:40,635
Satan is a clear

29
00:00:40,635 --> 00:00:42,109
enemy to man.

30
00:00:42,109 --> 00:00:43,073
And he told him

31
00:00:43,073 --> 00:00:44,506
something more.

32
00:00:44,803 --> 00:00:46,602
Your Lord will choose you,

33
00:00:46,602 --> 00:00:47,252
and teach

34
00:00:47,252 --> 00:00:48,971
you the meaning of events,

35
00:00:48,971 --> 00:00:50,526
and complete His favor

36
00:00:50,526 --> 00:00:51,304
on you

37
00:00:51,304 --> 00:00:54,072
and on the family of Yaqub.

38
00:00:54,183 --> 00:00:55,065
But the brothers

39
00:00:55,065 --> 00:00:56,633
already felt it.

40
00:00:56,633 --> 00:00:58,049
Yusuf and his brother

41
00:00:58,049 --> 00:00:58,920
are more beloved

42
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:00,394
to our father than we are,

43
00:01:00,394 --> 00:01:01,091
they said,

44
00:01:01,091 --> 00:01:03,209
and we are a strong group.

45
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:04,951
So they made a plan.

46
00:01:04,992 --> 00:01:06,072
Kill Yusuf,

47
00:01:06,072 --> 00:01:07,047
or throw him out

48
00:01:07,047 --> 00:01:08,742
to some far land,

49
00:01:08,742 --> 00:01:10,332
and your father's attention

50
00:01:10,332 --> 00:01:12,323
will be yours alone.

51
00:01:12,736 --> 00:01:13,815
One of them said:

52
00:01:13,815 --> 00:01:15,394
Do not kill Yusuf.

53
00:01:15,394 --> 00:01:16,219
Throw him into

54
00:01:16,219 --> 00:01:17,496
the bottom of the well,

55
00:01:17,496 --> 00:01:18,843
and some travelers will

56
00:01:18,843 --> 00:01:19,946
pick him up.

57
00:01:19,946 --> 00:01:21,757
They went to their father.

58
00:01:21,757 --> 00:01:22,360
Why do

59
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:24,601
you not trust us with Yusuf?

60
00:01:24,601 --> 00:01:26,133
Send him with us tomorrow,

61
00:01:26,133 --> 00:01:27,654
to eat and to play.

62
00:01:27,654 --> 00:01:29,129
We will guard him.

63
00:01:29,129 --> 00:01:30,603
Yaqub said:

64
00:01:30,603 --> 00:01:31,683
It saddens me

65
00:01:31,683 --> 00:01:33,018
that you would take him,

66
00:01:33,018 --> 00:01:33,738
and I fear

67
00:01:33,738 --> 00:01:35,212
a wolf would eat him while

68
00:01:35,212 --> 00:01:36,803
you are not watching.

69
00:01:36,803 --> 00:01:37,929
They took him,

70
00:01:37,929 --> 00:01:38,800
and they agreed

71
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:39,717
to put him into

72
00:01:39,717 --> 00:01:41,382
the bottom of the well.

73
00:01:41,493 --> 00:01:42,944
And in that moment,

74
00:01:42,944 --> 00:01:45,527
Allah inspired the boy:

75
00:01:45,731 --> 00:01:46,660
one day you will

76
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:48,111
tell them about this,

77
00:01:48,111 --> 00:01:48,749
and they will

78
00:01:48,749 --> 00:01:50,554
not know who you are.

79
00:01:50,758 --> 00:01:52,256
That night they came

80
00:01:52,256 --> 00:01:53,451
back to their father,

81
00:01:53,451 --> 00:01:54,571
weeping.

82
00:01:54,775 --> 00:01:55,924
We went racing,

83
00:01:55,924 --> 00:01:56,772
they said,

84
00:01:56,772 --> 00:01:57,945
and left Yusuf

85
00:01:57,945 --> 00:01:59,117
with our things,

86
00:01:59,117 --> 00:02:00,871
and a wolf ate him.

87
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:02,159
They brought his shirt,

88
00:02:02,159 --> 00:02:04,191
stained with false blood.

89
00:02:04,191 --> 00:02:06,211
Yaqub said: No,

90
00:02:06,211 --> 00:02:07,569
your souls have tempted

91
00:02:07,569 --> 00:02:09,032
you into something.

92
00:02:09,032 --> 00:02:11,401
So patience is most fitting.

93
00:02:11,401 --> 00:02:12,179
And Allah

94
00:02:12,179 --> 00:02:13,119
is the one whose

95
00:02:13,119 --> 00:02:14,552
help is sought.

96
00:02:15,104 --> 00:02:16,185
At the well,

97
00:02:16,185 --> 00:02:18,611
a caravan stopped for water.

98
00:02:18,611 --> 00:02:19,819
Their water drawer let

99
00:02:19,819 --> 00:02:20,771
down his bucket,

100
00:02:20,771 --> 00:02:22,036
and called out:

101
00:02:22,036 --> 00:02:22,791
Good news!

102
00:02:22,791 --> 00:02:24,277
Here is a boy.

103
00:02:24,277 --> 00:02:24,950
They hid him

104
00:02:24,950 --> 00:02:26,732
as goods to trade.

105
00:02:26,773 --> 00:02:27,713
And they sold him

106
00:02:27,713 --> 00:02:28,979
for a small price,

107
00:02:28,979 --> 00:02:30,946
a few silver coins.

108
00:02:31,057 --> 00:02:32,206
The man who bought

109
00:02:32,206 --> 00:02:33,216
him in Egypt

110
00:02:33,216 --> 00:02:34,609
was a great official,

111
00:02:34,609 --> 00:02:37,245
called al-Aziz in the Quran.

112
00:02:37,245 --> 00:02:38,661
He said to his wife:

113
00:02:38,661 --> 00:02:40,797
Make his stay comfortable.

114
00:02:40,797 --> 00:02:42,678
Perhaps he will benefit us,

115
00:02:42,678 --> 00:02:43,514
or we will take

116
00:02:43,514 --> 00:02:44,768
him as a son.

117
00:02:44,768 --> 00:02:46,277
And so Allah settled

118
00:02:46,277 --> 00:02:47,845
Yusuf in the land.

119
00:02:47,845 --> 00:02:49,470
When he reached maturity,

120
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:50,410
Allah gave him

121
00:02:50,410 --> 00:02:52,320
wisdom and knowledge.

122
00:02:52,361 --> 00:02:53,580
Then came his first

123
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:54,915
great test.

124
00:02:54,915 --> 00:02:56,320
The wife of al-Aziz,

125
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:57,539
in whose house he lived,

126
00:02:57,539 --> 00:02:59,176
tried to seduce him.

127
00:02:59,176 --> 00:03:00,801
She closed the doors.

128
00:03:00,801 --> 00:03:02,078
Yusuf said:

129
00:03:02,078 --> 00:03:04,087
I seek refuge in Allah.

130
00:03:04,087 --> 00:03:05,492
He is my master,

131
00:03:05,492 --> 00:03:07,396
and he has treated me well.

132
00:03:07,396 --> 00:03:09,839
The wrongdoers never succeed.

133
00:03:09,950 --> 00:03:11,053
Allah turned

134
00:03:11,053 --> 00:03:12,666
evil away from him.

135
00:03:12,666 --> 00:03:13,026
He was

136
00:03:13,026 --> 00:03:13,827
one of Allah's

137
00:03:13,827 --> 00:03:15,430
chosen servants.

138
00:03:15,430 --> 00:03:16,962
Yusuf ran for the door,

139
00:03:16,962 --> 00:03:18,541
and she ran after him.

140
00:03:18,541 --> 00:03:19,656
She tore his shirt

141
00:03:19,656 --> 00:03:20,550
from the back,

142
00:03:20,550 --> 00:03:21,339
and at the door

143
00:03:21,339 --> 00:03:22,721
stood her husband.

144
00:03:22,721 --> 00:03:24,741
She accused Yusuf at once.

145
00:03:24,741 --> 00:03:25,415
But a witness

146
00:03:25,415 --> 00:03:27,249
from her own family said:

147
00:03:27,249 --> 00:03:28,155
If his shirt

148
00:03:28,155 --> 00:03:29,745
is torn from the front,

149
00:03:29,745 --> 00:03:31,440
she is telling the truth.

150
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:32,276
If it is torn

151
00:03:32,276 --> 00:03:33,240
from the back,

152
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,656
she is lying.

153
00:03:34,656 --> 00:03:35,759
The shirt was torn

154
00:03:35,759 --> 00:03:36,972
from the back.

155
00:03:37,083 --> 00:03:39,684
Al-Aziz said: Yusuf,

156
00:03:39,684 --> 00:03:41,170
let this pass.

157
00:03:41,170 --> 00:03:42,563
And to his wife:

158
00:03:42,563 --> 00:03:45,145
ask forgiveness for your sin.

159
00:03:45,256 --> 00:03:46,464
But the story spread

160
00:03:46,464 --> 00:03:47,590
through the city.

161
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:48,542
So she invited

162
00:03:48,542 --> 00:03:49,656
the women who spoke

163
00:03:49,656 --> 00:03:50,434
about her,

164
00:03:50,434 --> 00:03:51,015
and gave

165
00:03:51,015 --> 00:03:52,478
each of them a knife.

166
00:03:52,478 --> 00:03:53,476
When Yusuf came

167
00:03:53,476 --> 00:03:54,626
out before them,

168
00:03:54,626 --> 00:03:56,007
they were so amazed

169
00:03:56,007 --> 00:03:56,727
that they cut

170
00:03:56,727 --> 00:03:58,039
their own hands.

171
00:03:58,039 --> 00:03:59,397
This is no human being,

172
00:03:59,397 --> 00:04:00,233
they said.

173
00:04:00,233 --> 00:04:02,497
This is a noble angel.

174
00:04:02,497 --> 00:04:03,263
She threatened

175
00:04:03,263 --> 00:04:04,424
him with prison.

176
00:04:04,424 --> 00:04:05,690
Yusuf prayed:

177
00:04:05,690 --> 00:04:06,676
My Lord,

178
00:04:06,676 --> 00:04:07,663
prison is dearer

179
00:04:07,663 --> 00:04:08,116
to me

180
00:04:08,116 --> 00:04:10,095
than what they call me to.

181
00:04:10,136 --> 00:04:12,394
And his Lord answered him.

182
00:04:12,435 --> 00:04:14,304
So Yusuf, innocent,

183
00:04:14,304 --> 00:04:15,999
was sent to prison.

184
00:04:15,999 --> 00:04:17,486
Two young men entered

185
00:04:17,486 --> 00:04:18,902
the prison with him.

186
00:04:18,902 --> 00:04:19,808
One dreamed

187
00:04:19,808 --> 00:04:21,712
he was pressing wine.

188
00:04:21,712 --> 00:04:22,675
The other dreamed

189
00:04:22,675 --> 00:04:24,347
he carried bread on his head,

190
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:25,113
and birds

191
00:04:25,113 --> 00:04:26,750
were eating from it.

192
00:04:26,750 --> 00:04:27,841
Before he explained

193
00:04:27,841 --> 00:04:28,991
their dreams,

194
00:04:28,991 --> 00:04:31,371
Yusuf called them to Allah.

195
00:04:31,371 --> 00:04:32,056
O my two

196
00:04:32,056 --> 00:04:33,739
companions of prison,

197
00:04:33,739 --> 00:04:34,796
are many separate

198
00:04:34,796 --> 00:04:35,945
lords better,

199
00:04:35,945 --> 00:04:36,978
or Allah,

200
00:04:36,978 --> 00:04:37,744
the One,

201
00:04:37,744 --> 00:04:39,068
the Prevailing?

202
00:04:39,068 --> 00:04:40,601
Then he told them.

203
00:04:40,601 --> 00:04:41,750
One of you will serve

204
00:04:41,750 --> 00:04:43,903
wine to his master again.

205
00:04:43,944 --> 00:04:45,918
The other will be crucified,

206
00:04:45,918 --> 00:04:47,126
and birds will eat

207
00:04:47,126 --> 00:04:48,431
from his head.

208
00:04:48,693 --> 00:04:49,111
He said

209
00:04:49,111 --> 00:04:51,027
to the one who would go free:

210
00:04:51,027 --> 00:04:53,307
Mention me to your master.

211
00:04:53,476 --> 00:04:55,531
But Satan made him forget,

212
00:04:55,531 --> 00:04:56,634
and Yusuf stayed

213
00:04:56,634 --> 00:04:58,903
in prison for several years.

214
00:04:58,991 --> 00:05:01,597
Then the king had a dream.

215
00:05:01,766 --> 00:05:03,727
Seven fat cows eaten

216
00:05:03,727 --> 00:05:05,272
by seven lean ones,

217
00:05:05,272 --> 00:05:06,537
and seven green

218
00:05:06,537 --> 00:05:07,942
ears of grain,

219
00:05:07,942 --> 00:05:09,788
and others dry.

220
00:05:09,788 --> 00:05:11,344
His advisers said:

221
00:05:11,344 --> 00:05:13,375
These are mixed-up dreams.

222
00:05:13,375 --> 00:05:14,536
And at last,

223
00:05:14,536 --> 00:05:15,024
the man

224
00:05:15,024 --> 00:05:15,883
from the prison

225
00:05:15,883 --> 00:05:17,578
remembered Yusuf.

226
00:05:17,578 --> 00:05:19,134
Yusuf explained it.

227
00:05:19,134 --> 00:05:20,376
Seven years you will

228
00:05:20,376 --> 00:05:21,781
farm as usual.

229
00:05:21,781 --> 00:05:23,243
Leave what you harvest

230
00:05:23,243 --> 00:05:24,416
in its ears,

231
00:05:24,416 --> 00:05:26,320
except a little to eat.

232
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:27,667
Then seven hard

233
00:05:27,667 --> 00:05:28,921
years will come,

234
00:05:28,921 --> 00:05:30,894
and eat what you stored.

235
00:05:30,894 --> 00:05:31,730
Then a year

236
00:05:31,730 --> 00:05:33,709
of relief will come.

237
00:05:34,122 --> 00:05:35,434
The king said:

238
00:05:35,434 --> 00:05:37,048
Bring him to me.

239
00:05:37,048 --> 00:05:38,162
But Yusuf would

240
00:05:38,162 --> 00:05:39,694
not leave prison until

241
00:05:39,694 --> 00:05:41,459
his name was cleared.

242
00:05:41,459 --> 00:05:42,666
Ask about the women

243
00:05:42,666 --> 00:05:43,851
who cut their hands,

244
00:05:43,851 --> 00:05:44,791
he said.

245
00:05:44,791 --> 00:05:46,103
The women said:

246
00:05:46,103 --> 00:05:48,286
We know no evil of him.

247
00:05:48,286 --> 00:05:50,910
And the wife of al-Aziz said:

248
00:05:50,910 --> 00:05:52,930
Now the truth is clear.

249
00:05:52,930 --> 00:05:53,696
It was I

250
00:05:53,696 --> 00:05:55,252
who tried to seduce him,

251
00:05:55,252 --> 00:05:57,156
and he is truthful.

252
00:05:57,156 --> 00:05:58,421
The king said:

253
00:05:58,421 --> 00:06:00,128
Today you are established

254
00:06:00,128 --> 00:06:00,848
with us,

255
00:06:00,848 --> 00:06:02,264
and trusted.

256
00:06:02,264 --> 00:06:03,663
Yusuf said:

257
00:06:03,704 --> 00:06:04,865
Put me in charge

258
00:06:04,865 --> 00:06:06,038
of the storehouses

259
00:06:06,038 --> 00:06:07,315
of the land.

260
00:06:07,315 --> 00:06:09,486
I am a knowing guardian.

261
00:06:09,486 --> 00:06:10,078
The boy

262
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:11,541
from the well now held

263
00:06:11,541 --> 00:06:13,334
the food of Egypt.

264
00:06:13,445 --> 00:06:15,070
The hard years came,

265
00:06:15,070 --> 00:06:15,767
and reached

266
00:06:15,767 --> 00:06:17,706
Yusuf's family too.

267
00:06:17,706 --> 00:06:18,751
His brothers came

268
00:06:18,751 --> 00:06:20,225
to Egypt for grain,

269
00:06:20,225 --> 00:06:22,025
and entered upon him.

270
00:06:22,025 --> 00:06:23,151
He knew them.

271
00:06:23,151 --> 00:06:24,776
They did not know him.

272
00:06:24,776 --> 00:06:26,263
He gave them full measure,

273
00:06:26,263 --> 00:06:27,226
and said:

274
00:06:27,226 --> 00:06:28,167
Next time,

275
00:06:28,167 --> 00:06:29,328
bring me your brother

276
00:06:29,328 --> 00:06:30,674
from your father.

277
00:06:30,674 --> 00:06:31,475
Without him,

278
00:06:31,475 --> 00:06:33,576
there is no grain for you.

279
00:06:33,576 --> 00:06:34,946
Yaqub said:

280
00:06:34,946 --> 00:06:36,502
Should I trust you with him,

281
00:06:36,502 --> 00:06:37,419
as I trusted

282
00:06:37,419 --> 00:06:39,126
you with his brother before?

283
00:06:39,126 --> 00:06:40,136
But Allah

284
00:06:40,136 --> 00:06:41,541
is the best guardian,

285
00:06:41,541 --> 00:06:42,179
and He

286
00:06:42,179 --> 00:06:43,665
is the most merciful

287
00:06:43,665 --> 00:06:45,016
of the merciful.

288
00:06:45,016 --> 00:06:46,514
They swore by Allah

289
00:06:46,514 --> 00:06:47,965
to bring him back.

290
00:06:47,965 --> 00:06:48,709
In Egypt,

291
00:06:48,709 --> 00:06:50,497
Yusuf took his brother aside,

292
00:06:50,497 --> 00:06:51,228
and said:

293
00:06:51,228 --> 00:06:52,749
I am your brother.

294
00:06:52,749 --> 00:06:53,922
Do not grieve over

295
00:06:53,922 --> 00:06:55,529
what they used to do.

296
00:06:55,695 --> 00:06:56,845
Then Yusuf placed

297
00:06:56,845 --> 00:06:58,145
the king's measuring cup

298
00:06:58,145 --> 00:06:59,712
in his brother's bag.

299
00:06:59,712 --> 00:07:01,036
It was found there,

300
00:07:01,036 --> 00:07:02,046
and by the brothers'

301
00:07:02,046 --> 00:07:03,102
own judgment,

302
00:07:03,102 --> 00:07:05,470
his brother stayed in Egypt.

303
00:07:05,470 --> 00:07:06,724
The eldest refused

304
00:07:06,724 --> 00:07:07,920
to go home.

305
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,046
The others returned

306
00:07:09,046 --> 00:07:10,695
and told their father.

307
00:07:10,695 --> 00:07:12,471
Yaqub said again:

308
00:07:12,471 --> 00:07:14,584
Patience is most fitting.

309
00:07:14,584 --> 00:07:16,001
Perhaps Allah will bring

310
00:07:16,001 --> 00:07:17,951
them all back to me.

311
00:07:17,951 --> 00:07:20,122
He turned away and said: Oh,

312
00:07:20,122 --> 00:07:22,084
my sorrow for Yusuf.

313
00:07:22,084 --> 00:07:23,338
His eyes turned

314
00:07:23,338 --> 00:07:24,929
white with grief.

315
00:07:24,929 --> 00:07:25,857
He said:

316
00:07:25,857 --> 00:07:27,413
I only complain of my

317
00:07:27,413 --> 00:07:29,526
grief and sorrow to Allah.

318
00:07:29,526 --> 00:07:30,710
My sons,

319
00:07:30,710 --> 00:07:31,546
go and search

320
00:07:31,546 --> 00:07:32,986
for Yusuf and his brother,

321
00:07:32,986 --> 00:07:34,042
and never despair

322
00:07:34,042 --> 00:07:35,928
of relief from Allah.

323
00:07:36,039 --> 00:07:37,003
The brothers came

324
00:07:37,003 --> 00:07:38,176
to Egypt again,

325
00:07:38,176 --> 00:07:39,964
poor and humbled.

326
00:07:39,964 --> 00:07:41,531
Yusuf asked them:

327
00:07:41,531 --> 00:07:42,193
Do you know

328
00:07:42,193 --> 00:07:42,913
what you did

329
00:07:42,913 --> 00:07:44,852
to Yusuf and his brother?

330
00:07:44,852 --> 00:07:45,850
They said:

331
00:07:45,850 --> 00:07:47,812
Are you really Yusuf?

332
00:07:47,812 --> 00:07:48,706
He said:

333
00:07:48,706 --> 00:07:49,589
I am Yusuf,

334
00:07:49,589 --> 00:07:51,098
and this is my brother.

335
00:07:51,098 --> 00:07:51,887
Allah has been

336
00:07:51,887 --> 00:07:53,332
gracious to us.

337
00:07:53,443 --> 00:07:54,314
They said:

338
00:07:54,314 --> 00:07:55,847
Allah has truly preferred

339
00:07:55,847 --> 00:07:57,112
you over us,

340
00:07:57,112 --> 00:07:58,935
and we were sinners.

341
00:07:58,935 --> 00:07:59,945
Yusuf said:

342
00:07:59,945 --> 00:08:01,791
No blame on you today.

343
00:08:01,791 --> 00:08:03,382
Allah will forgive you,

344
00:08:03,382 --> 00:08:03,811
and He

345
00:08:03,811 --> 00:08:05,088
is the most merciful

346
00:08:05,088 --> 00:08:06,389
of the merciful.

347
00:08:06,389 --> 00:08:07,213
He said:

348
00:08:07,213 --> 00:08:08,374
Take my shirt,

349
00:08:08,374 --> 00:08:09,396
and cast it over

350
00:08:09,396 --> 00:08:10,777
my father's face.

351
00:08:10,777 --> 00:08:12,472
He will see again.

352
00:08:12,472 --> 00:08:14,550
As the caravan left Egypt,

353
00:08:14,550 --> 00:08:15,793
Yaqub said:

354
00:08:15,793 --> 00:08:17,743
I can smell Yusuf.

355
00:08:17,743 --> 00:08:18,707
And when the shirt

356
00:08:18,707 --> 00:08:20,634
was cast over his face,

357
00:08:20,634 --> 00:08:22,341
his sight came back.

358
00:08:22,341 --> 00:08:23,409
The whole family

359
00:08:23,409 --> 00:08:24,767
came to Egypt.

360
00:08:24,767 --> 00:08:26,311
Yusuf raised his parents

361
00:08:26,311 --> 00:08:27,774
up onto the throne,

362
00:08:27,774 --> 00:08:28,842
and they all bowed

363
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:29,817
before him,

364
00:08:29,817 --> 00:08:30,897
as the stars,

365
00:08:30,897 --> 00:08:31,570
the sun

366
00:08:31,570 --> 00:08:32,847
and the moon had

367
00:08:32,847 --> 00:08:34,182
in his dream.

368
00:08:34,182 --> 00:08:35,541
Yusuf said:

369
00:08:35,541 --> 00:08:36,748
O my father,

370
00:08:36,748 --> 00:08:37,991
this is the meaning

371
00:08:37,991 --> 00:08:40,312
of my dream from long ago.

372
00:08:40,312 --> 00:08:41,334
My Lord has made

373
00:08:41,334 --> 00:08:42,484
it come true.

374
00:08:42,484 --> 00:08:43,645
And he prayed:

375
00:08:43,645 --> 00:08:45,131
Creator of the heavens

376
00:08:45,131 --> 00:08:46,152
and the earth,

377
00:08:46,152 --> 00:08:47,615
You are my protector

378
00:08:47,615 --> 00:08:49,856
in this world and the next.

379
00:08:49,856 --> 00:08:50,704
Let me die

380
00:08:50,704 --> 00:08:52,387
as one who submits to You,

381
00:08:52,387 --> 00:08:53,153
and join me

382
00:08:53,153 --> 00:08:54,512
with the righteous.

383
00:08:54,512 --> 00:08:55,243
The well,

384
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:56,845
the false accusation,

385
00:08:56,845 --> 00:08:57,786
the prison,

386
00:08:57,786 --> 00:08:59,857
the long years of grief.

387
00:09:00,154 --> 00:09:01,466
In every one of them,

388
00:09:01,466 --> 00:09:02,395
Allah's plan

389
00:09:02,395 --> 00:09:04,322
was quietly at work.

390
00:09:04,322 --> 00:09:05,878
Patience, trust,

391
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:06,911
and forgiveness

392
00:09:06,911 --> 00:09:08,484
carried the day.

393
00:09:08,525 --> 00:09:09,744
In their stories

394
00:09:09,744 --> 00:09:10,661
there is a lesson

395
00:09:10,661 --> 00:09:12,774
for people of understanding.

396
00:09:12,774 --> 00:09:14,852
That is the story of Yusuf.
